# Definition of Done

> The standing bar every round clears before it moves from **Review** to
> **Complete**. Verified in the round's Check phase.

**Keep this file general.** Round-specific criteria belong in that round's
`## Check` section, not here — a DoD that accumulates per-round checklists
stops being read, which is how this file rots.

---

## Code

- [ ] Follows the conventions already in the codebase, not new ones
- [ ] No linting or formatting errors introduced
- [ ] No `TODO`/`FIXME` left without something tracking it

## Tests

- [ ] The existing suite passes
- [ ] New behaviour has tests, including the edge cases the plan named
- [ ] A bug fix has a test that fails without the fix

## Documentation

- [ ] User-facing docs updated if behaviour changed
- [ ] `.agents/` updated if the architecture or a convention changed
- [ ] What you could **not** verify is written down as plainly as what you could

## Integration

- [ ] Works end to end, not only in tests
- [ ] No regression in neighbouring behaviour
- [ ] The change is independently landable — it does not need the next round

---

An unticked box is a finding, not a failure. Record why it is unticked and
whether it blocks the round; a DoD that is always fully green is one nobody is
reading.
